
%9Syntax:%9

UNTKL %|[-server <tag>] [-mask ident|host|domain] [-dry] <user@host|nick>

%9Parameters:%9

    -server:     Connection tag; defaults to the server of the active
                 window.
    -mask:       Type of mask built from WHOIS when a nick is given (as in
                 TKL; default: tk_mask_type).
    -dry:        Preview: shows the UNTKLINE line and sends nothing.

    <user@host|nick>: The mask to remove, or a nick the script builds the
                 mask from via WHOIS.

    The -force option is accepted but has no effect with UNTKL.

%9Description:%9

    Removes a temporary K-line (UNTKLINE) on an ircd 2.11 server.
    A command of the tk.pl script.

    The server matches the mask literally, without wildcards: it must be
    identical to the mask set with TKLINE. The safest way is to copy it
    from /TKLIST. When a nick is given, the script warns that the mask
    built from WHOIS may differ (another mask type, a changed host).

    Requires IRC operator status unless tk_require_oper is OFF. The mask
    goes through the same format checks as in TKL; sending is logged to
    tk_audit.jsonl.

%9Examples:%9

    /UNTKL *bot@*.example.org
    /UNTKL -dry *@203.0.113.*
    /UNTKL -mask host spammer

%9See also:%9 KLIST, TK, TKL, TKLIST

